    "rulings": [
      {
        "answer": "No, you can't. ＜De-Digivolve  nocategory＞ (Trash up to nocategory cards from the top. You can't trash past level 3 cards.) is not considered an effect where a Digimon would leave the battle area.",
        "question": "Can I activate this card's [All Turns] effect and place 4 [Vemmon] at the bottom of their owners' decks to prevent it from leaving the battle area when this Digimon is affected by a ＜De-Digivolve  nocategory＞ (Trash up to nocategory cards from the top. You can't trash past level 3 cards.) effect?",
        "reference": "[1]"
      },
      {
        "answer": "\"When [...] would leave the battle area\" refers to when this Digimon is placed in the trash, returned to the hand/deck, placed in the security stack, moved to the breeding area, or placed under another card.",
        "question": "What does this card's \"When this Digimon would leave the battle area\" mean, exactly?",
        "reference": "[1]"
      },
      {
        "answer": "Yes, you can activate it when this Digimon is affected by effect that moves it to one of those areas.",
        "question": "Can I activate this card's [All Turns] effect and place 4 [Vemmon] at the bottom of their owners' decks to prevent it from leaving the battle area when this Digimon is returned to my deck or placed in my security stack?",
        "reference": "[1]"
      },
      {
        "answer": "No, it doesn't activate if it becomes your opponent's turn before your main phase.",
        "question": "Can I activate this card's [Start of Your Main Phase] effect if an effect at the start of my turn or during my unsuspend phase or breeding phase causes the memory counter to move to my opponent's side and it becomes my opponent's turn?",
        "reference": "[1]"
      }
    ]
